# Tracer: compiler top-level standard-set membership
#
# Before (not in the persistent compiler ledger):
# 1 $in N
# Former limitation: this route was exercised only by transient probes and a
# Rust regression, so `./compiler.sh check examples` did not protect its
# generated Lean output.
#
# Now: each verified top-level membership is emitted as an explicit Litex.In
# proposition. The complex-valued source numeral retains separate membership
# evidence for N, Z, Q, R, and C; its Lean type is never used as a replacement
# for Litex membership.
#
# Boundary: this adapter currently accepts natural numeral literals for
# N/Z/Q/R membership. Negative, fractional, and general expression membership
# require their own reviewed verifier certificate and emitter adapter.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -strict -runner -f lean/examples/5_AtomicMembership.lit
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh compile examples/5_AtomicMembership.lit
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh check examples

1 $in N
1 $in Z
1 $in Q
1 $in R
1 $in C
